.TH AD_ANIM_TEST 1 "2026-09-09" "ad 1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ad_anim_test \- test animation by taking per-op snapshots
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ad_anim_test
.I <oldfile>
.I <newfile>
.I <opsfile>
.RB [ --check-in-place ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ad_anim_test
tests the ANIMATION (intermediate states), not just the final output.
It takes a snapshot after EACH op using the C animator's
.B --seek
flag, and verifies:
.PP
.RS
1. The buffer never contains garbage (no chars at wrong positions)
.br
2. Content is deleted in place (not joined to another line first)
.br
3.
.B join_lines
only happens on empty lines (all content already deleted)
.RE
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --check-in-place
Enable in-place deletion checks. Verifies that content deletes happen
at the correct line number (not after a join moved content to a
different line). Also checks that
.B join_lines
only happens on empty lines.
.SH WHY THIS IS NEEDED
L1/L2 (
.BR ad_l1l2 )
only tests the final output: old + ops = new. It cannot detect visual
issues like content jumping between lines before being deleted.
.PP
.B ad_anim_test
catches these issues by checking the buffer state after each op.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Test a simple animation:
.B ad_anim_test old.py new.py ops.tsv
.TP
Test with in-place checks:
.B ad_anim_test old.py new.py ops.tsv --check-in-place
.TP
Test with a layer chain:
.B ad_postprocess --ad-layer=ad_layer_reorder --ad-layer=ad_layer_line_delete_in_place < raw.tsv > post.tsv
.br
.B ad_anim_test old.py new.py post.tsv --check-in-place
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ad (1),
.BR ad_l1l2 (1),
.BR ad_postprocess (1),
.BR ad_session (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Written by the ad contributors.
